    "title": "All Rolling Stones Data Posts, January 21 2026",
    "text": "All Rolling Stones Data Posts, January 21 2026\nClick on title links to read all posts published today.\nIf you like what I do, help keep it going! ROLLING STONES DATA is a fan’s page for fans, ad-free, not affiliated to the band, and it runs on the support of readers like you. Your donation helps cover costs and keeps fresh Stones content coming your way. Thank you!\nRolling Stones chronology: January 21\nJanuary 21 has been a significant date in Rolling Stones history, marked by iconic performances, media events, and tributes, showcasing the band’s influence and presence across decades and continents.‘Where the Boys Go’: The Rolling Stones’ Punk Rocker (1980)\n‘Where the Boys Go’ by the Rolling Stones captures late 1970s British youth culture through cheeky lyrics and a raw sound, reflecting the band’s engagement with punk and pub rock trends while showcasing playful storytelling.Los Rolling Stones y ‘2000 Light Years from Home’ (1967)\nMick Jagger escribió ‘2,000 Light Years From Home’ en prisión convirtiendo su angustia en lírica psicodélica. La canción es un viaje cósmico que explora la soledad y la expansión de la conciencia.The Rolling Stones Say ‘I Don’t Know The Reason Why’ (1969)\nThe Rolling Stones’ unreleased track ‘I Don’t Know the Reason Why’, recorded in 1969, showcases raw blues energy with Mick Taylor’s guitar and Bobby Keys’ sax, representing the band’s experimental phase.The Rolling Stones Live Were More Dangerous (1968)\nKeith Richards asserts that The Rolling Stones’ live performances embody greater rebellion than their song ‘Street Fighting Man’, focusing on attitude over lyrics, creating electrifying chaos and defiance.Keith Richards on His Music Style (1975)\nKeith Richards described his guitar style as “bashing away,” emphasizing passion over technicality. He focused on rock’s roots, connecting with fans through raw energy and authenticity after Brian Jones’ death.\nCATEGORIES (updated daily):Today in Stones’ History (Daily chronology 1962-present)Can You Hear the Music? (All official songs 1963-present with song details, recording info, historical facts, and more)Flashback (The Stones live through the years)Unreleased (Lost and found! Unreleased songs 1962-present with recording info, song details, and more)Watch This All Together (Lost and found footage through the years)Articles (assorted pieces on the band)Yesterday’s Papers (The Stones in the press 1962-present)Stones Quotes (quotes from the boys through the years)\nAlso: Subscribe to Stones Data on Facebook here",
